---
description: Business content rules for services, recipes, articles and testimonials
alwaysApply: false
globs:
  - "src/**/*"
  - "supabase/**/*"
---

# Homepage

The homepage section order is fixed:

1. Hero
2. Short about section
3. Services
4. Yael's approach
5. Testimonials
6. Certificates
7. Recent articles
8. Recent recipes
9. Contact CTA
10. Footer

The administrator may edit content but may not reorder sections.

The Hero includes:

- Main title
- Subtitle
- Required primary button
- Optional secondary button
- Image, animation or video

# Services

Each service includes:

- Title
- Slug
- Short description
- Full introduction
- Cover image
- Target audience list
- Benefits list
- Process steps
- Optional FAQ
- Related testimonials
- CTA title
- CTA text
- CTA button
- External or internal link
- SEO fields
- Featured flag
- Status

List items support add, edit, remove and drag-and-drop ordering.

# Recipes

Each recipe includes:

- Title
- Slug
- Description
- Cover image
- Up to 6 additional media items
- Category
- Tags
- Preparation duration
- Servings
- Difficulty
- Ingredients
- Preparation steps
- Optional Yael tip
- Featured flag
- SEO fields
- Status

Do not create a separate recipe summary field.

Recipe cards use a shortened version of the description.

Ingredients and steps are dynamic ordered lists.

Related recipes are selected automatically by category or tags.

# Articles

Each article includes:

- Title
- Slug
- Rich content
- Cover image
- Optional media gallery
- Category
- Tags
- Automatic reading time
- Featured flag
- SEO fields
- Status

Related articles are selected automatically by category or tags.

# Testimonials

Testimonials do not use star ratings.

Each testimonial includes:

- Name
- Optional city
- Content
- Optional service relation
- Featured flag
- Published state

The homepage displays one testimonial at a time in a carousel.

Long testimonials show a "קראי עוד" action.

# Certificates

Each certificate includes:

- Title
- Organization
- Optional year
- Image
- Optional description
- Display order

# Contact Form

Fields:

- Full name, required
- Email, required
- Phone, optional
- Message, required
- Privacy policy checkbox, required

The form must state that users should not submit medical or sensitive information.

After submission:

- Save the message in Supabase.
- Send an email to Yael through Resend.
- Show a success message.
- Do not send an automatic email to the visitor.